{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update6.json\",\"summary\":\"Bound the removed-leader ReadIndex finding with a same-cause control and requested one execution. Change this turn: the harness assurance_singleton_test.go now also runs the identical two-voter removal inside a three-voter cluster, so the reduced configuration keeps two voters and the singleton shortcut cannot apply to the removed leader, and the comparison set keeps the earlier single-voter scenario (5 comparisons) while adding 5 for the control. The control was verified natively: after the removal node 1 is still StateLeader with config voters=(2 3), is_voter false and singleton false while the new leader of {2,3} has committed index 4 against the removed leader's 2; the same read then produces no answer at all (read_states 0, read_answered false) and instead enters the readOnly round (2 heartbeats carrying a read context, unconfirmed_reads 1), and three further heartbeat intervals with no reply leave it unanswered with unconfirmed_reads still 1 - so the stale immediate answer is specific to the single-voter remainder, and the same missing membership check has a second symptom, an accepted read that nothing inside raft can confirm. No interpretation was added this turn, so the question's recorded account is unchanged until this receipt exists; the expected outcome is that the control comparisons hold and the unconfirmed-read comparisons are violated.\"}"}}
